# Nancy CVE suppression file — one entry per line, format: CVE-ID until=YYYY-MM-DD
# Lines starting with # are comments.  Entries expire automatically on the until= date;
# once lapsed the scan fails again, forcing a re-review.
#
# Policy: only suppress CVEs where no fixed upstream release exists and the finding
# is therefore unactionable.  Every entry must name the affected package and document
# why bumping is not possible.  Re-check each entry when the weekly dependency scan
# runs (dependency-pin-check.yml / refresh-pins skill) or when a new release of the
# affected package appears.

# CVE-2026-56860 — golang.org/x/net
# Affected package : golang.org/x/net v0.58.0 (indirect dependency)
# Reason           : v0.58.0 is the newest release published upstream as of 2026-08-15;
#                    there is no patched version to upgrade to.  `go list -m -versions
#                    golang.org/x/net` ends at v0.58.0.  Re-check when a newer release
#                    appears or when this entry lapses on the expiry date below.
# Expiry           : 2026-11-15 — after this date the scan re-opens automatically.
CVE-2026-56860 until=2026-11-15

# CVE-2026-56859 — golang.org/x/net
# Affected package : golang.org/x/net v0.58.0 (indirect dependency)
# Dependency path  : github.com/openbao/openbao/api/v2 → golang.org/x/net/http2
# Reason           : v0.58.0 is the newest release published upstream as of 2026-08-19;
#                    `go list -m -versions golang.org/x/net` ends at v0.58.0 and
#                    `go list -m -u golang.org/x/net` reports no available update.
#                    There is no patched version to upgrade to.
#                    `govulncheck ./...` reports "No vulnerabilities found" — the
#                    affected DecodeElement code path is unreachable from our binaries.
#                    Note: the CVE describes `DecodeElement` depth-counter behaviour,
#                    which reads like an encoding/xml issue rather than an x/net one;
#                    the attribution may be an OSS Index artifact.  The suppression
#                    rests on "no patched release exists" plus the govulncheck result,
#                    not on doubting the attribution.  Re-check when a newer release
#                    appears or when this entry lapses on the expiry date below.
# Expiry           : 2026-11-15 — after this date the scan re-opens automatically.
CVE-2026-56859 until=2026-11-15
